  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The prayer that joins the offering to the saints — Our Lady, Ioseph, the twelve, and twelve martyrs of the Roman church: the popes Linus, Cletus, Clement, Sixtus and Cornelius, the bishop of Carthage Cyprian, the deacon Lawrence, Chrysogonus, John and Paul, Cosmas and Damian. The list is a single chain of genitives depending on memóriam venerántes, and every name in it is tagged genitive on that syntax, since several of the forms could as well be nominative plural. COMMUNICÁNTES at w001 and VENERÁNTES at w004 are nominative plural masculine, agreeing with a subject the sentence never states: the priest and those with him. IOSEPH at w021 is indeclinable and carries no declension; its case is the one beáti agrees with. GENETRÍCIS at w011 is the reading of the typical edition and of witness do; witness handmissal-eo prints Genitrícis, and both are real spellings of the word, so the difference is ruled in the apparatus rather than passed over. ÓMNIBUS at w069 is neuter — in all things, not among all men. CLETI at w046, COSMÆ at w056 and DAMIÁNI at w058 are unknown to both analyzers; their parses rest on the edition alone and say so in their provenance. MÁRTYRUM at w029, LINI at w045 and CLEMÉNTIS at w047 rest on Collatinus alone, because Whitaker's fails at each in a way his own dictionary explains: a genitive singular for mártyrum, which that form cannot carry (the singular is mártyris) — a porting artefact; flax, linum, in place of the pope Linus; and only the adjective clemens where the pope's name stands. None of the three is a question about the Latin, and the overrulings are recorded in the pipeline's rulings.",
    "source": {
      "method": "Verified by collation against the independent witnesses below: zero substantive divergence; the one genuine spelling variant (Genetrícis/Genitrícis) and the accidental variants are adjudicated in the apparatus. The typical edition itself (witness mr) agrees with this text at every token, punctuation included.",
      "witnesses": "witnesses/ordinarium.communicantes/",
      "apparatus": "witnesses/ordinarium.communicantes/apparatus.json"
    },
